  "rule": "A colour-1 divider (a full row/column, or an L boxing a corner) separates a legend of coloured key shapes from grey (5) blobs. Each key has a distinct number of enclosed holes (4-connected background regions inside the object's bounding box that do not touch its edge). Every grey blob is recoloured to the key with the same hole count, or erased to 0 if no key matches. The divider is not a key, and everything else is unchanged.",
  "scope": "Supported: grids 18-30 per side by default and 16-30 explicitly; all sizes other than 30x30 are synthetic extensions. Divider layouts are straight (full row/column, train 1 and both tests) and corner/L-shaped (train 2), with the legend on any of the four edges. A corner can sit at either end of its edge, giving 8 corner orientations. Each scene has 2-4 keys with distinct hole counts 0-6, using the fixture key template (3-thick bar with single-cell holes) and distinct colours from {1,2,3,4,6,7,8,9}; colour 1 keys are allowed. Each scene has 4-8 irregular eroded grey blobs (up to 10 explicitly) with hole counts 0-6, and every key count appears on at least one blob. Near-miss distractor blobs, which get erased, are included. Explicit controls are width, height, side, key_holes, key_colours, blob_holes and divider. Deliberately not supported: non-template key shapes (all fixture keys use the bar template), multiple dividers, non-zero background, keys that are not hole-count distinct, single-key legends, and corner scenes with 0-hole blobs but no 0-hole key, because there the L divider would be an ambiguous 0-hole colour-1 'key'. Fixture replay uses input_grid decomposition because the hand-drawn blobs are impractical to write as latent arguments.",
  "constraints": [
    "1200 independent padded-complement hole-count checks; all original fixtures exact",
    "516 corner dividers including 449 with zero-hole keys; 1170 unmatched blobs correctly erased; hole counts zero through six exercised",
    "Nine successful parameter controls and 15 invalid rejections; four old expectations now violate the documented requirement for two distinct key counts"
  ],
  "known_limitations": [
    "Keys always use the fixture bar template. Only grey blobs are irregular.",
    "Corner scenes never contain a 0-hole blob without a 0-hole key. This is an ambiguity guard, not a fixture-derived restriction.",
    "Fixture replay goes through input_grid decomposition rather than explicit latent arguments.",
    "The hole count range is capped at 6 and the number of blobs at 10.",
    "Grid sizes other than 30x30 are synthetic extensions.",
    "Bounded semantic checks do not prove coverage of every valid configuration."
